   "text": "Board of Supervisors Pima County Meeting Agenda MEETING LOCATION Administration Bldg - East 130 W. Congress Street 1st Floor Tucson, AZ 85701 Public Access to Hearing Room at 1:10 p.m. Board of Supervisors' Hearing Room 1:30 PM Tuesday, August 11, 2026 Study Session PIMA COUNTY BOARD OF SUPERVISORS Jennifer Allen, Chair, District 3 Dr. Matt Heinz, Vice Chair, District 2 Rex Scott, Member, District 1 Steve Christy, Member, District 4 Andrés Cano, Member, District 5 AGENDA/ADDENDUM AND BROADCAST INFORMATION At least 24 hours before each scheduled meeting, the agenda/addendum is available online at www.pima.gov and in the Clerk of the Board’s Office, 130 W. Congress Street, 1st Floor, Tucson, AZ 85701, Mon-Fri, 8am to 5pm. Cable Channels: Cox 96 Webcast: www.pima.gov PUBLIC COMMENTS Written comments to the Board of Supervisors regarding the agenda items can be submitted to COB_mail@pima.gov. All comments will be provided to the Board of Supervisors. HEARING ROOM NOTICE Law permits that a video and/or audio recording of all or part of this meeting may be made if doing so does not interfere with the conduct of the meeting. Pima County has no control over the use and distribution of any such recordings. In addition to the official meeting proceedings, these recordings may include images of and comments made by the public prior to the start, during a recess and after adjournment of the meeting, and may be posted on social media or other internet sites. ACCESSIBILITY The Board Hearing Room is wheelchair and handicapped accessible. Any person who is in need of special services (e.g., assistive listening device, Braille or large print agenda material, signer for hearing impaired, accessible parking, etc.) due to any disability will be accommodated. Please contact the Clerk of the Board at (520) 724-8449 for these services at least three (3) business days prior to the Board Meeting. Page 1 Pima County Printed on 8/10/2026\nAugust 11, 2026 Board of Supervisors Meeting Agenda Clerk's Note: Members of the Pima County Board of Supervisors will attend either in person or by telephone, video or internet conferencing. The meeting can be streamed via the following links: BOS Agenda August 11, 2026 (http://pima.granicus.com/ViewPublisher.php?view_id=3), on YouTube (https://www.youtube.com/c/PimaCountyArizona/), or via Cox Cable Channel 96. Television viewing will be available in the lobby at 130 West Congress, 1st Floor. 1. ROLL CALL 2. AGENDA ADJUSTMENTS EXECUTIVE SESSION (Clerk's Note: As of the posting date of 8/5/26, no executive session item has been placed on the study session agenda. However, this is subject to any addendum. Pursuant to A.R.S. §38-431.03(A)(3) the Board of Supervisors, or the Board sitting as other boards, may vote to go into executive session for the purpose of obtaining legal advice from its counsel with respect to any item listed on this agenda or any addendum thereto.) BOARD OF SUPERVISORS 3. UNFINISHED BUSINESS (6/9/26 and 7/14/26) Staffing Processes and Vacancy Policy 1. Discussion with County Administrator and Deputy County Administrators as to how staffing requests are analyzed and discussed with elected officials and department directors during the annual budgeting process. Also, discussion with same as to how staffing is discussed and monitored by administration throughout the rest of the year. 2. Discussion with County Administrator and Deputy County Administrators regarding the existing vacancy policy, how/why its current version was developed and if revisions to the current version should be considered. (District 1) BOS_StaffingProcessesVacancyPolicy_Dist1Submittal BOS_StaffVacPolQuestions_Dist1Submittal_7-8-26 BOS_StaffingProcessesVacancyPolicy_Slides_7-9-26 BOS_CAMemo_StaffingVacancyPolicy_7-31-26 BOS_VacanctPositionsPolicyUpdate_Slides_8-6-26 Attachments: 4. Board of Supervisors Representative Updates on Boards, Committees and Commissions and Any Other Municipalities Page 2 Pima County Printed on 8/10/2026\nAugust 11, 2026 Board of Supervisors Meeting Agenda COUNTY ADMINISTRATOR 5. Update on County Initiatives to Address Homelessness and Public Safety CA_CAMemo_OnePimaFY26Summary CA_OnePimaFY26Update_Slides Attachments: 6. Pima County Climate Action Update Update of Pima County’s Climate Action Plan, as requested by the Board of Supervisors. CA_CAMemo_ClimateActionUpdate_Slides_8-5-26 Attachments: 7. Wildfire Mitigation Plan One-Year Update Presentation/Discussion: One-year Update of the Wildfire Mitigation Plan. CA_CAMemo_WildfireMitigationPlan1YrUpdate CA_CAMemo_WildfireMitigationPlanAnnualUpdate CA_WildfireMitigationPlan1YrUpdate_Slides Attachments: FINANCE AND RISK MANAGEMENT 8. Monthly Financial Update Discussion regarding a monthly financial update on the County's financial performance. FN_MonthlyFinancialUpdate_Slides_8-6-26 FN_CAMemo_FinancialUpdateJul_8-7-26 Attachments: 9. ADJOURNMENT POSTED: 130 W. Congress Street, 1st Floor Tucson, AZ 85701 Pima County Homepage: www.pima.gov DATE/TIME POSTED: 8/5/26 @ 3:00 p.m. DATE/TIME REPOSTED (additional attachments only): 8/5/26 @ 4:30 p.m. DATE/TIME REPOSTED (amended meeting time, 1:30 p.m.): 8/6/26 @ 5:00 p.m. DATE/TIME REPOSTED (additional attachments only): 8/7/26 @ 8:45 a.m. DATE/TIME REPOSTED (additional attachments only): 8/7/26 @ 3:15 p.m. DATE/TIME REPOSTED (combined Agenda/Addendum): 8/10/26 @ 5:00 p.m. Page 3 Pima County Printed on 8/10/2026\nAugust 11, 2026 Board of Supervisors Meeting Agenda ADDENDUM 1 EXECUTIVE SESSION 1. Pursuant to A.R.S. §38-431.03(A)(3), for legal advice and discussion regarding Constable discipline. PCA_ExecSession-ConstableDiscipline Attachments: HUMAN RESOURCES 2. Recognition of the “We A.R.E. Gems” Quarterly Recipients Pursuant to Administrative Procedure 23-5, Employee Recognition Program, the following employees have been selected for the quarterly \"We A.R.E. Gems\" recognition: · Devin Robles - Library · Jennifer Seigla - Pima County Attorney’s Office · Alex Du Pont - Assessor Office · Jennifer Black - Human Resources · Hunter Tantlinger - Parks & Recreation · Barbara Geonaga - Conservation Lands & Resources · Sydney Harrington - Public Defense Services · Nichole Casebeer - Regional Flood Control District · Carlos Aguila - Library HR_RecognitionWeA.R.E.GemsQrtrlyRecipients Attachments: POSTED: 130 W. Congress Street, 1st Floor Tucson, AZ 85701 Pima County Homepage: www.pima.gov DATE/TIME POSTED: 8/7/26 @ 11:00 a.m. Page 4 Pima County Printed on 8/10/2026",
