   "text": "Agenda Page 1 of 3 March 24 th Township Council Regular Meeting As of: 3/24/2026 ROCKAWAY TOWNSHIP REGULAR MEETING AGENDA VIEW ON YOUTUBE HERE MARCH 24th, 2026 7:00PM 1. CALL TO ORDER 2. COUNCIL PRESIDENT TO LEAD THOSE PRESENT IN THE SALUTE TO THE AMERICAN FLAG 3. MOMENT OF SILENCE TO REMEMBER THE SERVICE AND SACRIFICES OF THE ARMED SERVICE MEMBERS WHO PROTECT OUR NATION AND THE FIRST RESPONDERS WHO PROTECT OUR NEIGHBORHOODS 4. ROLL CALL 5. ADEQUATE NOTICE OF THIS MEETING WAS PROVIDED TO THE DAILY RECORD AND THE OFFICIAL NEWSPAPERS FOR THE TOWNSHIP OF ROCKAWAY. NOTICE WAS POSTED ON THE OFFICIAL BULLETIN BOARDS OF ROCKAWAY TOWNSHIP, THE TOWNSHIP WEBSITE, AND NOTICE WAS FILED IN THE OFFICE OF THE TOWNSHIP CLERK. 6. APPROVAL OF MINUTE(S): A. MARCH 10 TH TOWNSHIP COUNCIL MEETING MINUTES 7. OPEN TO THE PUBLIC: 8. INTRODUCTION OF THE 2026 MUNICIPAL BUDGET A. O-26-08 ORDINANCE TO EXCEED THE MUNICIPAL BUDGET APPROPRIATION LIMITS AND TO ESTABLISH A CAP BANK (N.J.S.A. 40A: 4-45.14) B. RESOLUTIONS: I. R-26-67 A RESOLUTION TO INTRODUCE THE 2026 MUNICIPAL BUDGET OF THE TOWNSHIP OF ROCKAWAY IN THE COUNTY OF MORRIS II. R-26-68 RESOLUTION FOR SELF-EXAMINATION OF THE 2026 MUNICIPAL BUDGET III. R-26-72 RESOLUTION ESTABLISHING A POLICY FOR COMPREHENSIVE ONLINE PUBLIC DISCLOSURE OF MUNICIPAL BUDGET DOCUMENTS\nAgenda Page 2 of 3 March 24 th Township Council Regular Meeting As of: 3/24/2026 9. ORDINACE(S) FOR INTRODUCTION: A. O-26-09 BOND ORDINANCE APPROPRIATING $4,248,890, AND AUTHORIZING THE ISSUANCE OF $3,268,595 BONDS OR NOTES OF THE TOWNSHIP, FOR VARIOUS IMPROVEMENTS OR PURPOSES AUTHORIZED TO BE UNDERTAKEN BY THE TOWNSHIP OF ROCKAWAY, IN THE COUNTY OF MORRIS, NEW JERSEY. B. O-26-10 BOND ORDINANCE APPROPRIATING $1,730,000, AND AUTHORIZING THE ISSUANCE OF $1,690,000 BONDS OR NOTES OF THE TOWNSHIP, FOR VARIOUS IMPROVEMENTS OR PURPOSES AUTHORIZED TO BE UNDERTAKEN IN AND BY THE TOWNSHIP OF ROCKAWAY, IN THE COUNTY OF MORRIS, NEW JERSEY, FOR THE WATER SUPPLY AND DISTRIBUTION SYSTEM OF THE TOWNSHIP. C. O-26-11 ORDINANCE PROVIDING FOR IMPROVEMENT OF VARIOUS ROADS IN AND BY THE TOWNSHIP OF ROCKAWAY, IN THE COUNTY OF MORRIS, NEW JERSEY, AND REAPPROPRIATING $750,000 THEREFOR FROM PROCEEDS OF OBLIGATIONS OF THE TOWNSHIP HERETOFORE ISSUED AND FUNDS AVAILABLE UNDER ORDINANCES OF THE TOWNSHIP HERETOFORE ADOPTED. D. O-26-12 AN ORDINANCE FIXING THE SALARIES OF VARIOUS OFFICIALS AND CONTRACTUAL EMPLOYEES OF THE TOWNSHIP OF ROCKAWAY IN THE COUNTY OF MORRIS E. O-26-13 AN ORDINANCE FIXING THE SALARIES OF VARIOUS OFFICIALS AND NON-CONTRACTUAL EMPLOYEES OF THE TOWNSHIP OF ROCKAWAY IN THE COUNTY OF MORRIS 10. CONSENT AGENDA: R-26-63 AUTHORIZING THE CANCELLATION AND REFUND OF PROPERTY TAXES FOR HOMEOWNER QUALIFYING AS AN 100% DISABLED, TAX EXEMPT VETERAN R-26-64 A RESOLUTION AUTHORIZING REDEMPTION OF TAX TITLE LIEN C#25-00026 AGAINST BLOCK 20701 LOT 6.01 KNOWN AS 13 ALGONQUIN AVENUE R-26-65 AUTHORIZING THE CANCELLATION AND REFUND OF PROPERTY TAXES FOR HOMEOWNER QUALIFYING AS AN 100% DISABLED, TAX EXEMPT VETERAN R-26-66 REVOKING RESOLUTIONS R-25-53 AND R-24-169 AND SUPPORTING THE LOCATION AND OPERATION OF A CLASS 5 CANNABIS RETAILER BY KIND KUSH ROCKAWAY TOWNSHIP LLC WITHIN THE TOWNSHIP OF ROCKAWAY R-26-69 A RESOLUTION AUTHORIZING THE TRANSFER OF FUNDS R-26-70 AUTHORIZING THE CANCELLATION AND REFUND OF PROPERTY TAXES FOR HOMEOWNER QUALIFYING AS AN 100% DISABLED, TAX EXEMPT VETERAN\nAgenda Page 3 of 3 March 24 th Township Council Regular Meeting As of: 3/24/2026 R-26-71 A RESOLUTION AUTHORIZING THE AWARD OF A CONTRACT TO RIVERVIEW PAVING, INC. FOR THE CONSTRUCTION OF ROADWAY IMPROVEMENTS TO RESERVOIR ROAD – SECTION II IN THE TOTAL BID AMOUNT OF $459,015.52 11. NEW BUSINESS AND DISCUSSION: ALEJANDRO JIMENEZ-FONTANA – FULL MEMBERSHIP - Fire Company #4 COUNCIL REPORTS: Council Member Royek- Attended the March 18th BOE meeting. The spelling bee winners were announced and given certificates. A paraprofessional was awarded and given recognition for her work with children with autism. They announced their tentative budget that could cause a 6.69% tax increase. Council Member Wojtowicz- The Wildcat Ridge Preserve, a 123-acre wooded tract in Rockaway Township, has officially been preserved as open space following a sale closing on a project funded through a $1.04 million grant from the Morris County Open Space Preservation Trust Fund. The grant, approved by the Morris County Board of County Commissioners, enabled The Land Conservancy of New Jersey to secure the property. The closing on March 12, 2026, represents the first finalization of purchases involving three open space grants approved in November, authorizing nearly $7 million to preserve 192.3 acres across three municipalities. Council Member Kelley - On March 11th, I attended the Water Department building name dedication/celebration. On March 16th, I visited the areas of power loss, due to extremely high winds, in the Meriden and Valley Road sections of the 6th Ward. During my visit, I spoke with NG Gilbert and Verizon regarding power and communication restoration time frames. I Followed up with Police Chief Scheer regarding recorded data and speeding concerns on Decker/Lyonsville Road [still waiting for the recorded data]. I prepared for and participated in the March 14, 2026 public budget meeting. It was great to see many members of the public that attended. During the budget meeting I made many motions to cut over $300,000 of fat within the budget, increase revenues and public safety. However, the majority of council members were not interested in those areas of reductions to save taxpayer's money. 12. ADJOURNMENT: * NEXT TOWNSHIP COUNCIL REGULARY MEETING – APRIL 14TH*",
