0 A RESOLUTION AUTHORIZING REDEMPTION OF TAX TITLE LIEN C#25-00023 AGAINST BLOCK 11507.05 LOT 9 KNOWN AS 322 RICHARD MINE RD., E9. R-26-81 A RESOLUTION AUTHORIZING REDEMPTION OF TAX TITLE LIEN C#25-00030 AGAINST BLOCK 21003 LOT 30 KNOWN AS 309 BEACH ST. R-26-82 A RESOLUTION AUTHORIZING REDEMPTION OF TAX TITLE LIEN C#25-00037 AGAINST BLOCK 21604 LOT 31 KNOWN AS 28 HIBERNIA RD. R-26-83 A RESOLUTION AUTHORIZING REDEMPTION OF TAX TITLE LIEN C#25-00038 AGAINST BLOCK 21706 LOT 23 KNOWN AS 75 WHITE MEADOW RD. R-26-84 A RESOLUTION AUTHORIZING REDEMPTION OF TAX TITLE LIEN C#25-00039 AGAINST BLOCK 21909 LOT 1 KNOWN AS 15 NAVAJO WY. R-26-85 A RESOLUTION AUTHORIZING REDEMPTION OF TAX TITLE LIEN C#25-00040 AGAINST BLOCK 22003 LOT 2 KNOWN AS 11 ELLEN DR. R-26-88 AUTHORIZING THE AWARD OF A CONTRACT TO DEMAIO ELECTRICAL COMPANY, INC. FOR THE CONSTRUCTION OF FOX HILLS WELL FILTRATION IN THE TOTAL BID AMOUNT OF $1,180,000.00 R-26-89 A RESOLUTION AUTHORIZING REDEMPTION OF TAX TITLE LIEN C#25-00011 AGAINST BLOCK 11007 LOT 10 KNOWN AS 73 FALLEN TIMBERS TRL. R-26-90 AUTHORIZING THE AWARD OF A CONTRACT TO AJM CONTRACTORS INC. FOR THE CONSTRUCTION OF ROADWAY IMPROVEMENTS TO RESERVOIR ROAD – SECTION 1 IN THE TOTAL BID AMOUNT OF $415,265.60 12. NEW BUSINESS AND DISCUSSION:\nAgenda Page 4 of 5 April 28 th Township Council Regular Meeting As of: 4/28/2026 LIAM MUNN – JUNIOR MEMBERSHIP - Fire Company #4 DAVID CHO – FULL MEMBERSHIP - Fire Company #2 Utility Committee 13. COUNCIL REPORTS: Councilman Adam Salberg: Report on Open Space Trust Fund: March 30 re-org meeting. 2026 resident contribution: 5/8 cent per $100 of valuation in which 1/4 cent goes to county parks and open space 1/4 cent goes to historic preservation 1/8 cent goes to municipal and/or qualifiable conservancy. No Board of County Commissioners report. Councilwoman Sophia Freire: Councilwoman ’ s report for April 28, 2026 Safety of our roads -met with town engineer, head of DPW, Ms. Palmieri, and the police chief to discuss the health of our roads. -winter repair is in action -they work in sections -map to also based on concerns that are reported Notice a road issue report it online or contact the road garage at 973-627-1700. -Your concerns and reports about speeding and road health are very important to maintaining the roads themselves. -Traffic trailers collect important data about speeding and traffic, your concerns influence where they are needed. -MT Hope Ave and RD are major arteries and as such are under Morris County ’ s control. Issues with them should be reported to the Morris County ’ s DPW 973-285-6761. -Ask for the traffic sergeant on duty. -DPW investigates troubling trees. JCPNL cuts the trees by power lines -RAVE is an alert system about the roads that you can sign up for through the Rockaway website. -6-year plan in place for the roads, Feb-May is worst stress months for the roads. Council Member Kelley: I want to thank Mr. Knoth and Ms. Ferrante for assisting me with my concerns regarding a dangerous tree on Lake Denmark Road. Thank you to Officer Schwarzmann for assisting me\nAgenda Page 5 of 5 April 28 th Township Council Regular Meeting As of: 4/28/2026 with my concern of illegal dumping of construction debris on State Preservation Land off of Valley Road. Thank you to Officer Foster for assisting traffic regarding the downed tree on Green Pond Road. Thank you to the Morris County DPW (John Clark's crew) for addressing many pot holes on Green Pond Road. Thank you to the Recreation Department (Morgan Morris)for the preparation of the fields associated with youth sports programs. I attended the Hibernia Co.1 fishing contest on Opening Day hosted by the Co.1 Ladies Auxiliary and Co.1 Fire House. Stopped by the Township Library event which was well attended. I hope everyone had a wonderful Passover and Easter Holiday 14. ADJOURNMENT: * NEXT TOWNSHIP COUNCIL REGULARY MEETING – MAY 12TH*",
