   "sourceOrg": "Tucson Unified School District Governing Board",
   "collectedAt": "2026-08-14T03:15:45.987Z",
   "verifiedAt": null,
   "text": "Tucson Unified Governing Board Next Meeting View the Governing Board Meeting Live. Governing Board Meeting 8/25/2026 4:30pm - 8:30pm &times; Governing Board Meeting Date & Time: 8/25/2026 4:30pm - 8:30pm Governing Board meetings are held at the Duffy Community Center, 5145 E. 5 th Street, 85711, in the Multipurpose Room. All meeting notices, agendas, minutes, actions, recordings, and other resources are available on Diligent Community . Audio-video recordings are available shortly after the meetings also on Diligent Community . Close Board Members Dr. Ravi Shah Email Dr. Ravi Shah Board President Term expires: December 31, 2028 Natalie Luna Rose Email Natalie Luna Rose Board Clerk Term expires: December 31, 2028 Jennifer Eckstrom Email Jennifer Eckstrom Term expires: December 31, 2026 Val Romero Email Val Romero Term Expires: December 31, 2026 Sadie Shaw Email Sadie Shaw Term expires: December 31, 2028 Current Members' Bios Members: 1867-Present (PDF) Contact the Board Email Governing Board ( [email&#160;protected] ) Phone: (520) 225-6070 FAX: (520) 798-8767 Policies for Review: When the Governing Board is soliciting feedback on policies proposed for elimination, revision, and adoption, please click here to: Share your feedback Board Meeting The Governing Board will hold a Special Meeting on Tuesday, August 25, 2026 with Executive Session beginning at 4:30 p.m. and the Public meeting scheduled to begin at 5:30 p.m. at the Duffy Community Center - Multipurpose Room, 5145 E. Fifth Street, Tucson, AZ 85711. There will be a Public Hearing at the August 25th meeting for the Revision of Instructional Time Model (ITM) for Palo Verde High Magnet School Effective for the 2026-2027 School Year. Public access for each meeting will begin 15 minutes prior to the vote to go into Executive Session. Meeting notices are posted outside the front door at the TUSD District Office at 1010 E. Tenth Street, Tucson, AZ 85719. Call to the Audience The following procedures related to the Call to the Audience portion of Board meetings will be observed: Members of the public who wish to address the Board shall complete a Request to Address Board form and submit electronically to the Board office by noon the day of the meeting or physically to Board Staff at the start of the meeting before the close of Call to the Audience. Submission must include name of speaker, topic of comments and should indicate which agenda item your comments relate to. Submission must indicate whether individuals will address the Board in person or will submit written comments to be read into the record (email written comments to [email&#160;protected] ) by noon the day of the meeting. The complete rules for Call to the Audience are located in Governing Board Policy BEDH - Public Participation at Board Meetings, Policy-Code-BEDH (tusd1.org) . Se observar&aacute;n los siguientes procedimientos relacionados con la porci&oacute;n del Llamado a la Audiencia: Los miembros del p&uacute;blico que deseen abordar a la Mesa Directiva deben llenar la forma Petici&oacute;n para Dirigirse a La Mesa Directiva y someta esta forma electronicamente a la oficina de la Mesa Directiva para el mediodia el dia de la junta, o fisicamente al personal de la Mesa Directiva en la reuni&oacute;n en cualquier momento antes del cierre del Llamado a la Audiencia. Debe incluir su nombre, tema de los comentarios y debe incluir cu&aacute;l asunto de la agenda se relacionan sus comentarios. Debe indicar si desea dirigirse a la Mesa Directiva en persona o someter sus comentarios escritos para ser leidos (comentarios escritos pueden ser eviados por correo electr&oacute;nico al [email&#160;protected] ) para el mediodia del dia de la junta. Las reglas completes para la Llamado a la Audiencia pueden encontrar en la Pol&iacute;tica de la Mesa Directiva BEDH &ndash; Public Participation at Board Meetings, Policy-Code-BEDH (tusd1.org) . Meeting Materials Beginning January 13, 2026, Tucson Unified will be using Diligent Community to provide easy access to support materials, greater efficiency for the district, and increased transparency. To access agenda items and support materials go to Diligent Community . Recordings Audio-video recordings are available after the meetings on Diligent Community just choose the meeting you wish to view and then select video. Vacancies Events with 3 or More Members Impact Tucson Community and Family Resource Fair - July 25, 2026 Proclamations Resolutions National School Counseling Week Proclamation - February 2-6, 2026 Career & Technical Education (CTE) Month Proclamation - February 2026 Purchasing Month Proclamation - March 2026 Social Worker Month Proclamation - March 2026 Live Meeting Videos Governing Board meetings will be available here when meetings are in session. August 11, 2026 Meeting Vote to Convene On district Windows devices, students and staff may find that these videos on YouTube are blocked. If so, please log into Google with your district credentials . Error Message: For more details and instructions, please visit our TS Article on YouTube Videos (Sharepoint) . Thank you for your patience, as we work to resolve this.",
   "extraction": "html",
   "extractionNote": null
  },
